WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.800
Maya pays one hundred and twenty dollars once.

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:05.934
Her bank confirms one transaction.

00:00:06.855 --> 00:00:09.776
Then three order confirmation emails arrive, and the

00:00:09.803 --> 00:00:12.342
warehouse receives repeated shipping requests.

00:00:14.003 --> 00:00:16.989
The payment provider sends a signed success webhook.

00:00:17.913 --> 00:00:20.676
Our server processes it, but its acknowledgement is

00:00:20.703 --> 00:00:21.203
lost.

00:00:22.137 --> 00:00:24.926
The provider cannot tell whether processing finished.

00:00:26.603 --> 00:00:28.774
The provider retries the same event.

00:00:29.711 --> 00:00:32.500
An unsafe handler sends another email and shipment

00:00:32.526 --> 00:00:33.145
request.

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:36.447
The webhook reports an existing payment.

00:00:37.368 --> 00:00:39.513
It does not charge the customer again.

00:00:41.203 --> 00:00:44.689
First, verify the original request bytes, timestamp and

00:00:44.716 --> 00:00:45.242
merchant.

00:00:46.166 --> 00:00:49.245
Save the event identity in a durable PostgreSQL

00:00:49.271 --> 00:00:49.903
inbox.

00:00:50.824 --> 00:00:53.995
A repeated delivery is safely acknowledged without creating

00:00:54.021 --> 00:00:54.561
new work.

00:00:56.203 --> 00:00:58.887
A different event identifier can still describe the

00:00:58.900 --> 00:00:59.663
same payment.

00:01:00.574 --> 00:01:03.297
Transition pending to succeeded only once.

00:01:04.218 --> 00:01:06.692
A late success notification must never move a

00:01:06.705 --> 00:01:08.613
refunded payment back to succeeded.

00:01:10.269 --> 00:01:13.361
Commit the inbox, payment update and outbox intent

00:01:13.375 --> 00:01:15.927
in one database transaction, then acknowledge.

00:01:16.864 --> 00:01:19.548
A separate worker retries with stable email and

00:01:19.575 --> 00:01:20.614
fulfillment keys.

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:24.219
Downstream systems must deduplicate too.

00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:28.646
Now repeated webhooks receive a safe acknowledgement

00:01:28.672 --> 00:01:30.527
without repeating the business action.

00:01:31.464 --> 00:01:34.898
One payment, one logical confirmation, one fulfillment

00:01:34.911 --> 00:01:35.451
intent.

00:01:36.385 --> 00:01:39.517
Monitor failures and reconcile ambiguous outcomes.

00:01:40.451 --> 00:01:43.780
These are illustrative counts, not production measurements.
